Rajiv fashion, a reputed garment manufacturing unit needs to find its day-to-day expenses like
wages, rent, maintaining stock of raw material, etc. The owner approaches his raw material
supplier to give them credit for two months, so that he can get cloth for making garments
without making immediate payment. The supplier made an enquiry regarding Rajiv and found that
his reputation of giving payment is not very good. In past the lenders were not very happy.
(a) What source of finance Rajiv is trying to get in above case?
(b) Should the raw material supplier grant credit to Rajiv fashion house?
प्रारंभूBATCH
Answer
(a) Trade Credit
(b) No, as his past payment record is not good and he is not enjoying good reputation.
